# ETL Pipeline Using Python Generators and Pandas

## Project Overview

This project demonstrates a simple **ETL (Extract, Transform, Load)** pipeline built in Python. It processes a CSV dataset containing approximately **1,000 rows and 50 columns** of sample employee data.

The project focuses on **generator-based data extraction**, **data cleaning**, **loading data into a Pandas DataFrame**, and **analyzing memory usage**. It also compares the memory behavior of generator-based processing with the traditional `pandas.read_csv()` approach.

---

## Features

* Extract data using Python generators (`yield`)
* Clean and transform CSV data
* Load transformed data into a Pandas DataFrame
* Export cleaned data to a new CSV file
* Measure memory usage using `psutil`
* Compare generator-based processing with `pd.read_csv()`
* Demonstrate Python garbage collection

